  "details": "This is on VRChat Build 1160.\nDescription:\nAvatar elements containing cloth components seem to sporadically behave incorrectly (very stiff in sections, shape never corrects itself). This is not an issue with colliders or self-collision. I've been unable to ever reproduce this in my Unity editor, so I'm making the assumption that this is a client (or SDK?) bug.\nSteps to reproduce:\n1. Upon loading into any world, there appears to be some chance the \"stuck\" behaviour occurs. \n2. Alternately, toggling the cloth component on/off may trigger this behaviour as well.\n3. Pressing the 'Reset Avatar' button on the expressions menu seems to always correct it back to regular.\nExtra files:\nI've attached a video link demonstrating incorrect behaviour, followed by it corrected after pressing \"Reset Avatar\" on the radial menu. Note the strange scrunching around arms. This isn't collider issues, although I maybe don't demonstrate that too well:\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qIDqrpx1e5o",
